            %p
              The morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              is the composite
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi R
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi R
                    %mi Y
                    %mo →
                    %mi R
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P R f\to R X \times R Y \to R X
              at the top, which is a pullback of
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mi R
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P R Y \to R Y
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi P
                      %mi R
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mi Y
                      %mo ×
                      %mi R
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi R
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P R Y \to R Y \times R Y \to R Y
              = succeed ")," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mi Y
                      %mo →
                      %mi P
                      %mi R
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R Y \to P R Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi
              are acyclic fibrations. Moreover, since
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi π
                      %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi j
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pi i = j_X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-3"} 2-out-of-3
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              is also a weak equivalence.
            %p
              Now the projection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mi R
                    %mi f
                    %mo →
                    %mi P
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P R f\to P Y
              is a fibration, so since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is anodyne there is a lift
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi g
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
              in the second square as shown. Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi j
                      %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} j_Y
              are weak equivalences, by
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-out-of-6"} 2-out-of-6
              it follows that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a weak equivalence.
          %p Note that this condition also dualizes straightforwardly to the left-transferred case.
          %h3#ConstructingFactorizationsForLeftTransfer For left transfer
          %p
          #RecognitionOfLeftTransferUnderCofibrantlyGeneration.num_prop
            %h6 Proposition
            %p
              Given a pair of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functors"} adjoint functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒟
                    %munderover
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo ⊥
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mi R
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mi L
                    %mi 𝒞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathcal{D}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{R}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\overset{L}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\;\;\bot\;\;}
                    \\mathcal{C}
              such that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒟
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{D}
                  are
                  = succeed "," do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{C}
                  is equipped with the
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mathematical+structure"} structure
                  of a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} cofibrantly generated model category
                  (hence a
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/combinatorial+model+category"} combinatorial model category
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class"} classes
                  of (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibration"}> co
                  \-)/
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
                  and
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+equivalences"} weak equivalences
                  = succeed "," do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
