            %p
              The right-transfer along an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+equivalence"} adjoint equivalence
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
              always exists, and here also the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrations"} cofibrations
              are given by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/preimage"} preimage
              under
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
          This is straightforward to check directly, even without the above existence theorems (e.g.
          = succeed ")." do
            %a{:href => "https://math.stackexchange.com/a/2220718/58526"} math.se:a/2220718
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+functors"} projective model structure on functors
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi M
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^D
              is right-transferred from the product model structure on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi ob
                          %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{ob D}
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/injective+model+structure+on+functors"} injective model structure on functors
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi M
                        %mrow
                          %mi ob
                          %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M^{ob D}
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+algebraic+fibrant+objects"} model structure on algebraic fibrant objects
              is right-transferred from the underlying model category by forgetting the choice of fillers.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strict+2-monad"} strict 2-monad
              on a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+finitely+presentable+category"} locally finitely presentable 2-category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_s
              of strict
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra+over+a+monad"} algebras
              admits a right-transferred model structure from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-trivial+model+structure"} 2-trivial model structure
              on
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudolimits"} pseudolimits
              of arrows for path objects, and the (cofibration, trivial fibration) factorization is constructed using a version of the construction of Lemma
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#AlgebraicLift"}
              (since the 2-trivial model structure on
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
              may not be cofibrantly generated).
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counterexample"} counterexample
              is provided as Example 3.7 of (
              %a{:href => "#GoerssShemmerhorn07"}> Goerss &amp; Schemmerhorn 2007
              ). Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              be a field of characteristic 2 and consider the adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi CGA
                      %mi k
                    %mover
                      %munder
                        %mo →
                        %mi U
                      %mover
                        %mo ←
                        %mi S
                    %msub
                      %mi Ch
                      %mo *
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (S \dashv U )\; : \; CGA_k \stackrel{\overset{S}{\leftarrow}}{\underset{U}{\to}} Ch_*k
            %p
              of the symmetric algebra functor and the forgetful functor between graded commutative DGAs and chain complexes. One sees that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              does not preserve the weak equivalence between 0 and the complex with one copy of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              in degrees
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (S \dashv U )
              cannot be upgraded to a Quillen adjunction.
          %p
          .num_remark
            %h6 Example
            %p
              A more category-theoretic
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/counterexample"} counterexample
              is that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Reedy+model+structure"} Reedy model structure
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+graphs"} directed graphs
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
              to
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
              does not right-transfer to the category
              %span.newWikiWord
                DblCat
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/DblCat"} ?
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+categories"} double categories
              along the free-forgetful adjunction. One of the generatic trivial cofibrations for the Reedy model structure “transports” a horizontal arrow (in double-category terminology) along two vertical isomorphisms, which is a levelwise equivalence. But upon pushing out the free double category generated by this along a map into some other double category, new composite horizontal arrows may be generated in the codomain that are not isomorphic to the image of anything in the domain; thus the pushout is no longer a levelwise equivalence. So, the acyclicity condition fails.
          %h2#References References
          %p The explicit notion of right transfer is due to:
          %ul
            %li#Crans95
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sjoerd+Crans"}> Sjoerd Crans
              , §3-§4 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Quillen closed model structure for sheaves
              %strong 101
              1 (1995) 35-57 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0022-4049(94)00033-F"}> doi:10.1016/0022-4049(94)00033-F
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "http://citeseerx.ist.psu.edu/viewdoc/summary?doi=10.1.1.48.7459"} web
          %p
            and for the case of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+categories"} cofibrantly generated model categories
            due to:
          %ul
            %li#DwyerHirschhornKan97
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+G.+Dwyer"}> William G. Dwyer
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+S.+Hirschhorn"} Philip S. Hirschhorn
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+M.+Kan"} Daniel M. Kan
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Model+Categories+and+More+General+Abstract+Homotopy+Theory"} Model Categories and More General Abstract Homotopy Theory
              (1997) &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://people.math.rochester.edu/faculty/doug/otherpapers/dhk.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/DwyerHirschhornKan-ModelCategories.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p#FurtherReferencesForRightTransfer
            The existence result of right transfer due to
            %a{:href => "#Crans95"} Crans 1995, Thm. 3.3
            and
            %a{:href => "#DwyerHirschhornKan97"} Dwyer, Hirschhorn &amp; Kan 1997, Thm. 91
            (“Crans-Kan transfer theorem”) is reviewed/reworked, with variations, in:
          %ul
            %li#GoerssJardine99
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+F.+Jardine"} J. F. Jardine
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Simplicial+homotopy+theory"} Simplicial homotopy theory
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 174
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4"} doi:10.1007/978-3-0346-0189-4
            %li#Hirschhorn02
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Philip+Hirschhorn"}> Philip Hirschhorn
                , Thm. 11.3.2 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Model+Categories+and+Their+Localizations"} Model Categories and Their Localizations
                = succeed "," do
                  %strong 99
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/surv-99-s/"} ISBN:978-0-8218-4917-0
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.gbv.de/dms/goettingen/360115845.pdf"} pdf toc
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.maths.ed.ac.uk/~aar/papers/hirschhornloc.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Cisinski06
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Denis-Charles+Cisinski"}> Denis-Charles Cisinski
                , Prop. 1.4.23 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Les préfaisceaux comme types d’homotopie|Les préfaisceaux comme modèles des types d’homotopie
                %strong 308
                Soc. Math. France (2006), 392 pages &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item/?id=AST_2006__308__R1_0"}> numdam:AST_2006__308__R1_0
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.univ-toulouse.fr/~dcisinsk/ast.pdf"} pdf
            %li#GoerssShemmerhorn07
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Paul+Goerss"}> Paul Goerss
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kristen+Schemmerhorn"} Kristen Schemmerhorn
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/PS_cache/math/pdf/0609/0609537v2.pdf#page=20"} §3.2
                of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Model Categories and Simplicial Methods
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Interactions between Homotopy Theory and Algebra
                %strong 436
                AMS (2007) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.AT/0609537"}> arXiv:math.AT/0609537
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://dx.doi.org/10.1090/conm/436"} doi:10.1090/conm/436
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Axiomatic homotopy theory for operads
                %strong 78
                (2003) 4 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0206094"}> arXiv:math/0206094
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00014-003-0772-y"} doi:10.1007/s00014-003-0772-y
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "http://www.math.uu.nl/publications/preprints/1242.pdf"} pdf
          %p
            These arguments all go back (cf.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#GoerssShemmerhorn07"} Goerss &amp; Shemmerhorn 2007, p. 20
          %ul
            %li#Quillen67
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Quillen"}> Daniel Quillen
              , §II.4 in:
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Homotopical+Algebra"} Homotopical Algebra
              = succeed "," do
                %strong 43
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/BFb0097438"} doi:10.1007/BFb0097438
          %p The above proof of acyclicity in the presence of path objects is taken from:
          %ul
            %li#Rezk02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Rezk"}> Charles Rezk
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Every homotopy theory of simplicial algebras admits a proper model
              %strong 119
              1 (2002) 65-94 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/math/0003065"}> arxiv:math/0003065
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Discussion of left transfer (left-induced model structures):
          %ul
            %li#HessShipley14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"}> Kathryn Hess
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The homotopy theory of coalgebras over a comonad
                %strong 108
                2 (2014) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1205.3979"}> arXiv:1205.3979
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/plms/pdt038"} doi:10.1112/plms/pdt038
            %li#BHKKRS15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Marzieh+Bayeh"}> Marzieh Bayeh
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"} Kathryn Hess
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Varvara+Karpova"} Varvara Karpova
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Magdalena+Kedziorek"} Magdalena Kedziorek
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"} Emily Riehl
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Left-induced model structures and diagram categories
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Women in Topology: Collaborations in Homotopy Theory
                %strong 641
                American Mathematical Society (2015) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1401.3651"}> arXiv:1401.3651
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://bookstore.ams.org/conm-641"} ISBN:978-1-4704-2495-4
            %li#HKRS15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kathryn+Hess"}> Kathryn Hess
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Magdalena+Kedziorek"} Magdalena Kedziorek
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"} Emily Riehl
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Brooke+Shipley"} Brooke Shipley
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A necessary and sufficient condition for induced model structures
                %strong 10
                2 (2017) 324-369 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1509.08154"}> arXiv:1509.08154
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/topo.12011"} doi:10.1112/topo.12011
          %p
            Beware that
            %a{:href => "#HKRS15"} HKRS15
            contains an error, corrected by:
          %ul
            %li#GKR18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Garner"}> Richard Garner
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Magdalena+Kedziorek"} Magdalena Kedziorek
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emily+Riehl"} Emily Riehl
              = succeed "," do
                %em Lifting accessible model structures
              %strong 13
              1 (2020) 59-76 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.09889"}> arXiv:1802.09889
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1112/topo.12123"} doi:10.1112/topo.12123
          %p
            Technical lemmas regarding the underlying
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cellular+categories"} cellular categories
          %ul
            %li{:id => "MakkaiRosický14"}
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M.+Makkai"}> M. Makkai
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J.+Rosick%C3%BD"} J. Rosický
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Cellular categories
                %strong 218
                (2014) 1652-1664 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1304.7572"}> arXiv:1304.7572
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jpaa.2014.01.005"} doi:10.1016/j.jpaa.2014.01.005
            %li#Lurie09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacob+Lurie"}> Jacob Lurie
                , Appendix A of:
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higher+Topos+Theory"} Higher Topos Theory
                (2009)
          %p The right-transferred model structure on algebras for a 2-monad is from
          %ul
            %li#Lack06
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Steve+Lack"}> Steve Lack
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Homotopy-theoretic aspects of 2-monads
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math.CT/0607646"} arXiv
